    "exit_gate": "The executable M2 candidate supplies the neutral registry, durable lifecycle/recovery, immediate socket peer audit token/PID generation, double-sampled proc-generation ancestry, same-UID host barrier, split claim-set/resource/broker lifecycles, content-free terminal history, CLI/IPC, internal status/Canvas projections, and one registered microphone adapter. Public tap returns OPERATION_TAP_UNAVAILABLE before record creation because no tap source is registered; artifact reveal/remove/release/retain return OPERATION_ARTIFACT_CUSTODY_UNAVAILABLE before lookup or mutation because no production producer or custody adapter exists. Accepted tap and artifact lifecycle schemas remain target and durable-recovery truth, not executable success. The invocation-scoped external helper binding keeps the token parent-only, dynamically admits only the trusted Node.js Foundation signed image and mapped vnode, writes the exact reviewed entry/helper bytes through an in-memory module bundle after admission, finalizes tokenlessly from the exact child peer, and terminalizes abandoned, expired, boot-recovered, or failed prepared claims. It deliberately claims only the adapter-registry revision containing microphone: unadapted legacy daemon work, artifact-producing recording adapters, public SDK projections, and raw managed-tool transport remain later milestones. Each later adapter must join this same plane with exact list/inspect/status/recent, kill, cleanup, artifact/stream facts, and proof; asserted lineage continues only to narrow."
